WEBVTT

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:17.830
Wow!  He stood up again!

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.070
The duel isn’t over yet!

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.800
Yusaku!

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.000
So you’re not giving up on this duel.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.600
Secure Gardna can change 
battle damage to 0 once.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.480
But that’s not enough to 
completely stop my attack.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.720
Be quiet!  We know that!

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.720
So you can avoid it by other means?

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.720
What are you pinning your 
hopes on, Playmaker?

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.790
Simple.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.960
My determination.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:58.040
I'll fight this duel to the end and beat you!

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.800
I run Across the universe

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.970
At the speed of light

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.840
Begin Loading

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:24.570
Open the door of dreams

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:28.140
VRAINS spreads

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.250
Believe in myself

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.780
VRAINS continues

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:40.090
The circuit draws the future

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:44.160
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:45.760
Access!

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.460
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.060
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:52.370
Link with my soul

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.140
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.870
Now Win the Race

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:59.710
Connected world

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:03.210
No matter when

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:06.580
Nothing is impossible

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.720
Strive for hope

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:15.290
And ride the wind!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.760
That’s why you’re 
my archrival, Playmaker.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.970
I'll also use all my strength to the end!

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:38.040
Here I go!

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.670
My turn!  I draw!

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.650
There’s a set trap card 
on Playmaker’s field.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:51.410
But if I use Borreload and Borrelsword, 
I can seal away that card.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:54.380
Battle!  Borreload Dragon!

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.060
Attack Secure Gardna!

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.690
Charging energy!

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.930
Varrel mode change!

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.160
Target, locked on!

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.680
Final safety removed!

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.530
Thunder Varrel Cannon!

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.720
He’s targeting Secure Gardna!

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.940
But if we use a trap card...

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:23.410
Borreload’s effect now activates!

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.650
Anti Enemy Varrett!

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:30.160
One faceup monster loses 500 ATK and DEF.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.730
You can’t activate card 
effects against this effect!

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:38.090
I select Secure Gardna!

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:45.150
Since Disconnect Linker resurrected Secure 
Gardna, card effects can't affect it.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.290
So why did he choose it?

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.710
To seal away our card.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:54.820
Even if his effect doesn't work, I won't 
be able to activate card effects anymore.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.950
Seriously?  Anything goes for that punk!

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.360
Anti glare protection!

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.640
It's over!  Do it, Borreload!

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:08.530
Secure Gardna’s effect!

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:12.760
Once per turn, battle or 
effect damage becomes 0!

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:16.270
But now you have no monsters to defend you!

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:17.240
I’m not done!

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:21.750
Protection Wizard's effect 
activates from my graveyard!

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.200
What?

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:29.250
By banishing this card, Secure 
Gardna isn't destroyed!

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.590
In that case, Borrelsword attacks!

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.380
Borrelsword’s effect!

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:44.840
By switching a monster from attack to 
defense position, it can attack twice.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:49.500
You can’t activate card 
effects against this effect!

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.280
I select Magnarokket Dragon!

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:55.630
And Magnarokket’s effect!

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.680
It self-destructs to send one 
monster to the graveyard!

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.480
I select Anesthrokket!

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:09.920
But I now activate Cluster Congester’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:16.360
By banishing Cluster Congester from my 
graveyard and Secure Gardna from the field...

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:21.970
...I Special Summon Congester Tokens up to 
the number of Link Monsters on your field!

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.820
These Tokens are destroyed 
at the end of the turn...

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:31.140
...but you take 300 damage for each one!

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:33.920
We have five Tokens.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:38.350
If he can’t stop them, 
we'll deal 1500 damage.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:42.320
A cornered rat will bite the cat.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.050
Be quiet!  We'll defeat you!

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:50.240
Fine.  I’ll take them on.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.010
Borrelsword attacks Congester Token!

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:04.330
Borrelsword attacks another Congester Token!

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:08.820
Show me your special card, Playmaker!

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:12.910
I activate the trap, Transaction Rollback!

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:20.130
By halving my LP, it gains the effect 
of a Normal Trap in your graveyard!

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.930
I select Mirror Force!

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:36.360
All right!

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:39.740
Revolver only has monsters 
in attack position!

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:42.210
Too bad.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:46.960
Topologic Gumblar Dragon’s effect!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:53.320
When it’s Extra Linked, Link Monsters on 
my field can’t be destroyed by effects!

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:57.250
What?

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:02.670
See that?  This is Topologic Gumblar's 
power when it's Extra Linked!

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:06.000
You only had one way to make a comeback.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.920
So I knew you'd use my Mirror Force!

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:14.880
Let me get rid of those bothersome Tokens.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.520
Borrelsword!  Borrelguard!

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.860
Topologic Bomber!  Topologic Gumblar!

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:23.040
All attack!

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.500
I end my turn.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:43.480
Magnarokket’s effect 
activates from the graveyard.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.940
I Special Summon Autorokket Dragon.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:53.680
Due to Boot Sector Launch’s 
effect, it gains 300 ATK!

00:07:55.010 --> 00:08:00.130
We managed to survive this turn’s 
attacks, but we’re at the brink!

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:01.750
So will you give up?

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:03.440
Definitely no!

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:07.270
That’s right.  I can’t 
give up on this duel either.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.500
Umm, Playmaker?

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.020
What is it?

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:14.110
Please stop doing that 
out-of-character smile!

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:15.930
Be how you always are!

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.620
I’m at wit's end!

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.950
Fine.  I won’t smile anymore.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:25.420
Everything depends on this draw.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:29.400
My ten years…  And the 
future of the world…

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:31.560
My turn!

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:34.630
This is the draw that will lead to my future!

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.600
How'd you do, Playmaker?

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:45.840
I applaud you for stopping 
my attacks last turn.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:48.840
But this duel's outcome is set.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:53.320
Since I created the Extra 
Link, you can't win.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:55.790
Give up, Playmaker.

00:08:55.790 --> 00:09:00.760
You and that Ignis will perish with me!

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:07.810
Revolver, my heart has always been alone.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:10.230
I don’t even have one friend.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.370
It’s not like this is what I wanted.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.900
Even if I try to walk a 
different path, I can’t!

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:25.800
A deep abyss that can’t be crossed.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:30.010
A giant darkness that annihilates my world.

00:09:30.010 --> 00:09:33.980
That's how bad the incident 
tore apart my heart.

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:38.960
I can tell you my true feelings!

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:41.920
Even my suffering and my weaknesses!

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.200
What are you talking about?

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.870
You live in the same world as me!

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:49.700
Back then, you said…

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:54.910
Three.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.900
Think of three things.

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:02.730
You couldn't just stand by, 
so you crossed the abyss.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.820
You’re able to save me!

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.660
And I’m able to save you!

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:13.200
Are you serious, Playmaker?

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:18.130
If he becomes your friend, 
that means he'll be my friend?

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.120
That’s right!

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:30.000
I’ll never be your friend!  Is 
this how you beg for your life-

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.520
I’m not begging!

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.370
Then what are you doing?

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:37.590
I’ve already connected 
the circuit of victory!

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:38.950
What?

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:41.430
I was waiting for this, Playmaker!

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:45.420
Your life is like a candle in the wind.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:49.890
The Extra Link is already 
complete on my field.

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:53.220
And you only have one card in your hand.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:55.870
But you still think you can win?

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.870
That’s right!

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:07.640
So instead of begging for your 
life, you were showing me mercy?

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:10.640
No.  You’re the same as me.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:15.230
You said we’re prisoners of 
fate.  That you had no new path.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:18.600
But I believe there's still a new path!

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:24.060
I see.  Then prove it with your dueling!

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.800
#1: My revenge is over.

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:32.280
#2: I'll overcome the abyss 
of destiny in this duel!

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:36.920
#3: We'll seize a new future together!

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.480
Here I go, Revolver!

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:40.450
Bring it on, Playmaker!

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:45.590
I activate Transaction Rollback's 
effect from my graveyard!

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:49.400
By halving my LP, I banish this card!

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:56.120
That lets me activate the effect 
of a Normal Trap in my graveyard!

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:59.720
I activate Recoded Alive!

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:03.140
By banishing a Cyberse from my graveyard...

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:07.840
...I Special Summon a Code 
Talker from my Extra Deck!

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.580
I banish Transcode!

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.810
I Special Summon Encode Talker!

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:20.160
Playmaker hasn’t given up yet!

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:24.360
But now Topologic Gumblar’s effect!

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.160
Both our hands are entirely destroyed!

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:29.060
Unformed Card!

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:34.540
Now your only hope has vanished!

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:40.540
Wrong!  I used your monster’s 
effect to destroy my hand!

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:41.770
What?

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:46.520
I activate the effect of the Equip Spell 
that was sent to the graveyard - Spam Mail!

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:52.380
When it's sent from the hand to the 
graveyard, I draw a card and let you see it!

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:56.270
I drew a monster card, Swap Cleric!

00:12:56.270 --> 00:13:01.570
If you have faceup cards with the 
same Type as the card you saw...

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:05.100
...you select one of them 
and return it to your hand!

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.690
Want me to choose for you?

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:11.040
I return Autorokket to my hand.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.510
I summon Swap Cleric!

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:21.950
And I activate Recoded Alive’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:28.340
By banishing this card, I Special 
Summon a banished Code Talker!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:32.230
Return, Transcode Talker!

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.670
Transcode and Topologic Bomber have linked!

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:48.800
But Shield Handler has already 
negated Topologic Bomber’s effect!

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.410
Transcode’s effect!

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:55.130
Mutually linked monsters both gain 500 ATK!

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:59.740
Since a monster was Special 
Summoned next to a link...

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:01.850
...Topologic Gumblar’s effect activates.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:05.250
Only my entire hand is destroyed.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.930
Transcode’s additional effect!

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:13.890
I Special Summon a Code Talker from my 
graveyard next to this card’s link on my field!

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.740
Resurrect, Powercode Talker!

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:21.470
Transcode’s effect!

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:23.940
It gains 500 ATK!

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:29.360
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:31.720
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.790
The summoning conditions 
are at least two monsters.

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:40.490
I set Swap Cleric and Link 3 Encode 
Talker in the Link Markers!

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:45.330
Appear, Link 4 Firewall Dragon!

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:57.410
This is…

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:14.570
Awesome!

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:18.170
So this is what you were 
aiming for, Playmaker!

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:23.770
He used Revolver’s monsters 
to create an Extra Link!

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:26.740
Swap Cleric’s effect activates!

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:30.710
When Swap Cleric is used to Link 
Summon and sent to the graveyard...

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:37.190
...the Link Summoned monster loses 
500 ATK, and I draw one card.

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:41.430
Revolver, this is the true 
power of the Extra Link!

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:45.390
This card will lead us on a new path!

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:55.170
The Continuous Spell, Zero Extra Link!

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:02.640
For every monster that's Extra 
Linked, Transcode gains 800 ATK!

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.350
Wow!

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:09.260
Regardless of friend or foe, the 
linked monsters' powers converge!

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:14.490
Transcode gains 6400 ATK!

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:18.220
With this ATK, we can destroy 
Revolver and his Dragons!

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:22.200
I activate the trap, Link Short!

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:25.880
The effects of mutually linked monsters on your field

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.430
are negated and can’t attack this turn!

00:16:32.230 --> 00:16:35.840
Can’t attack?  Seriously?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:38.040
This match is now determined!

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:40.190
It’s not over yet!

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:43.720
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:44.680
What?

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:46.620
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:49.920
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Effect Monsters!

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:58.160
I set Transcode Talker, Powercode Talker 
and Firewall Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.100
Circuit combine!

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:02.130
Link Summon!

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:06.520
Appear, Link 3 Decode Talker!

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:13.040
Its effect activates!

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:15.250
Power Integration!

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:20.720
Since Decode Talker isn’t affected 
by Link Short, it can attack this turn!

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:23.690
But what can you do with that ATK?

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:26.790
Zero Extra Link’s additional effect!

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:30.660
When an Extra Linked monster 
is used to Link Summon...

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:36.670
...the Link Monster gains 
that monster's ATK increase!

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:42.850
What?

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:45.320
Go, Decode Talker!

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.610
Decode End!

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:09.000
He won…  He won!

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.480
Playmaker won!

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:13.950
Well done, Yusaku!

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.320
I lose, Playmaker.

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:26.020
Since I lost, the Tower of Hanoi stops.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:29.570
But remember this:

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:36.160
As long as the Ignis are a threat to 
humanity, I won't run from my destiny!

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:47.890
Boss!  The Tower of Hanoi has stopped!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.080
He did it, Sato!

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:52.190
The network world is saved!

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:54.150
Boss, that name…

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:57.830
Times like this, we can call 
each other by our names.

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:00.120
You always call me by my name.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.120
My name is Saito.

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:13.130
Everyone has been freed.

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:41.950
Yusaku!

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:44.210
Yusaku…

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:54.240
So Revolver left.

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:56.840
But he'll return someday.

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:00.670
To fulfill his purpose.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:09.800
Wow!  So this is the Stardust Road!

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:11.290
It’s beautiful.

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:17.720
What's that?

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.610
The lock’s removal program.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:20.640
What lock?

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:21.840
Yours.

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:25.940
You’re free.  Go wherever you like.

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.680
You’re freeing me?

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:33.140
Hanoi has perished.  Your role is over.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:35.600
Playmaker…

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.330
Go.  Before I change my mind.

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:43.810
In the human world, at times like this, I'm 
supposed to say something profound, right?

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:45.370
Are you capable?

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.840
One man’s fault is another’s lesson!

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:51.060
Nice words.

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:52.930
I’m awesome!

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:56.260
I’m leaving, Playmaker-  I mean, Yusaku.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:20:58.050
Yeah.  Be well.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:00.950
Ai.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.050
Leave the Duel Disk.

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:08.290
Oh yeah.  I don’t need 
the Duel Disk anymore.

00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:14.100
See you.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:17.760
Ai…

00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:23.830
He's gone.

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:33.860
Leaving already?

00:21:33.860 --> 00:21:34.740
Yeah.

00:21:35.150 --> 00:21:36.400
What about Ai?

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:38.890
He went home.

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:41.850
I see...  I'll drive you home.

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:43.820
No, it’s fine.

00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:15.400
My life is like detestably bad graffiti

00:22:15.760 --> 00:22:22.540
But when you looked at 
me, I felt I wasn't alone

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:29.740
I'm glad that I'm alive  I truly am

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:37.120
What I couldn't say before, I can say now

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:44.340
Within the sadness that I kept holding down

00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:48.490
There were fragments of power

00:22:48.730 --> 00:22:55.670
No one can take away my light to the future

00:22:55.900 --> 00:23:03.010
The chronicles of life only has a few lines

00:23:03.140 --> 00:23:10.220
People I meet, my regrets – they're 
all like ultramarine diamonds to me

00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:17.420
You've always confront loneliness by yourself

00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:24.300
I bet we can now laugh 
together, forever and ever

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:31.970
Lighting Life with our invisible bond

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:41.260
The heroes have stopped the Tower of Hanoi.

00:23:41.260 --> 00:23:47.440
But an incident occurs during the 
opening of the new LINK VRAINS.

00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:51.850
Hearing a sudden scream, Yusaku-

00:23:51.850 --> 00:23:54.720
No - Playmaker faces it!

00:23:55.220 --> 00:23:58.220
Who is that?

00:23:58.360 --> 00:24:02.920
Next time on YU-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Playmaker Returns

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:04.830
Into the VRAINS!
